# Keep user how-to pages current

When you ship a **user-visible** change (new control, new flow, changed behavior, or a new honest limit), update the broker-facing how-to **in the same commit** as the code. Do not push product changes that leave these pages describing the old app.

## Source of truth

1. `lib/page-guides.ts` — walkthrough + features per route. Feeds **How Beacon works** (`/how-beacon-works`) and the floating **?** button.
2. `app/how-beacon-works/page.tsx` — Day-1 path and **Honest limits** (not generated from page-guides).
3. `app/copilot/actions.ts` — Copilot “Beacon platform knowledge”. Brokers ask Copilot how to do things; stale text here is a product bug.

## What to change

- New or renamed button/flow on a screen → that screen’s `walkthrough` and `features` in `page-guides.ts`.
- New route → add a `PAGE_GUIDES` entry (and TOC category).
- New limitation (GIS cannot do X, listing search will not overwrite Y) → `features` / walkthrough **and** How Beacon works honest limits **and** Copilot “does NOT have”.
- Copilot “How to do common things” must use the same paths and button names as the UI.

Do not invent filters, menus, or send-email. If the product cannot do it, say so in the guide.

## Do not skip

A “docs later” commit is not allowed for user-facing behavior. If you are unsure which guide to edit, update the route the broker is standing on plus Copilot.
